Usage: tic [-e names] [-o dir] [-R name] [-v[n]] [-V] [-w[n]] [-1aCDcfGgIKLNrsTtUx] source-file

Terminfo compiler.

OPTIONS:
  -V             print version
  -a             retain commented-out capabilities
  -c             check only
  -o ARG         set output directory
  -v[=NUM]       set verbosity level
  -x             treat unknown capabilities as user-defined
      --help     display this help and exit
      --version  output version information and exit

EXIT STATUS:
  0  if OK,
  1  if minor problems,
  2  if serious trouble.

WinuxCmd is a Windows implementation of GNU CoreUtils for Linux-Windows developers and AI coding assistants.
